Z||000000||87FieroGTx||10-11-2001||02:29 PM|||| This is from Motor trend, It was in a Opal Speedster review.<P>""If the Opal Speedster is given the green light, we'd like to see the Fiero moniker brought back to life for the Speedster, with a turbocharged variant to wear a GT badge. The important message is that the Speedster proves GM can build daring, exciting vehicles that can execute their mission undiluted. And one we hope is on its way to a Pontiac dealer near you.""<P> One can only hope!||||reg||4
Z||000001||falconhulk||10-11-2001||02:33 PM||||Hope?  While I really like the speedster who here is likely to pay upwards of $30,000 for one?  They are cool looking cars but I would have to wait a few years for a used one.  If you want something along this line there are a number of foreign roadsters available in that price range already.  Lets face it this car is foreign right?  Just becasue it might have the Fiero badge does not make it a domestic.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||10-11-2001||02:34 PM||||This has been discussed, at length. Try doing a search on "Opel" or "Elise".<BR>One of the Forum members e-mailed Bob Lutz, a few days ago, regarding the Fiero.<BR>Supposedly, Lutz said to keep an eye out at the Detroit Auto Show. Not sure what that's supposed to mean, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-11-2001||03:41 PM||||Motor Trend wrote that at the tail end of a review of the Opel Speedster a while ago.  Really, they were just saying their wishful thoughts, but the as the Opel is right now you won't see it in this country.  It would need too many modifications, not to mention a new plant built to double its meager production capacity (its only like 2000 or 3000 a year right now!).<P>I would seriously doubt GM would resurrect the Fiero nameplate even on a two seat mid engined car.  We have all been asked by countless people about the Fiero's being death traps because they burn up.  The nameplate has a very bad reputation, and GM couldn't clean it up once.  They won't try again.||||reg||1
