Z||000010||falconhulk||10-12-2001||10:40 AM||||Yes its a midengined roadster but there are already a bunch out there.  This one is just not special.  If it was cheaper then the $30,000 base price it might be.  The Fiero was specail when it came out becasue it had a great price and gave everyman the ability to own a mid engined sports car that could handle up with the porsche.  Thi car is fantastic and I would love to have one but for me, when you leave the 20's you leave me behind.  Thing about cars like this is that they tnd to hold thier value so it might be a long time before a used one hits my sweet spot.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Screwie||10-12-2001||11:43 AM||||They should take the Opel badge off though, cause where I come from Opels aren't even considered cars (the styling of other Opels just s***s, and they drive like a tractor in the mud without wheels)<P>Just my $0.02 about Opel though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||10-12-2001||12:41 PM||||I think after ther car is seen... and is available to go look at and drive if it were to be produced... that it would be embraced.<P>I know the automotive press has said a Speedster would probably cost in the neighborhood of $30, but do you hink Saturn or Pontiac could sell a $30K roadster?  Of course not!  It would have to be price competative with the Mazda Miata and Toyota MR2.  If its pitted against higher cost roadsters like a Z3 or Honda S2000 its going to bomb.  I just don't see the market positions of either company (Saturn-Econony, Pontiac-A little more luxury than a Chevy which isn't saying much) pulling off a car that will compete with the expensive ones from a marketing standpoint.  Pontiac would have more of a chance, but Saturn would be hard pressed to market a high cost roadster with a dealers lot full of cars at the other end of the spectrum.<P>I say bring one on!  Whether its a Saturn roadster, or a Pontiac!  Show me where to sign!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||10-12-2001||12:57 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Screwie:<BR><B>They should take the Opel badge off though, cause where I come from Opels aren't even considered cars (the styling of other Opels just s***s, and they drive like a tractor in the mud without wheels)<P>Just my $0.02 about Opel though    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What about the Opel GT of the 70s?  My dad has a restored '73 Opel GT that is absolutely beautiful!  <P>And you can't downplay Opel's current styling too much.  Look at the Opel/Vuaxhall Omega- It's sold here with the V6 option as a rebadged Cadillac Catera. Even the Astra series isn't that bad to look at.  I'd be open to bringing back the Opel badge... I'm about 99% sure that won't happen, but I'd be open to it.  <P>When is the Detroit show anyway?<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
